  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technologies and digital innovations for inclusive learning in Eastern Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Although the relevance of technology in enhancing the resilience of education systems was revealed during the COVID-19 pandemic, many countries were not adequately prepared for the new mode of teaching and learning. They face many challenges. In response, UNESCO aims to steer the digital transformation of education and will support Member States in Eastern Africa in the following areas: (a) review, development and implementation of national ICT in education policies, (b) teacher training on the use of digital technology and ICT tools, (c) improvement of curricula for the integration and use of ICT in education, (d) improvement of ICT infrastructure and internet connectivity, and (e) bridging the gender digital divide. Intersectoral cooperation and cooperation with UNESCO Institutes and other development partners will be enhanced. Mobilization of extrabudgetary resources will also be strengthened.</narrative>
  </description>
